  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \nLittle change in the forecast through the weekend and into next\nweek as high pressure remains dominant across the Desert Southwest,\nwhich keeps monsoonal moisture shunted south of much of the Great\nBasin. A shortwave trough moves across the Pacific Northwest and \ninto the Northern Plains Sunday into Monday, leading to stronger \nafternoon wind gusts across northern Nevada with gusts from 25 to \n30 mph Saturday and Sunday afternoons. With minimum afternoon \nrelative humidity values in the single digits, elevated to \nlocalized critical fire weather condtions will develop across \nareas north of I-80 Saturday, Sunday, and Monday afternoons. \n\nThe other story will be the continued heat across northern and\ncentral Nevada with moderate to major HeatRisk values for max\nafternoon heat indices in the mid to upper 90s, especially in\nvalleys. Saturday will feature the hottest high temperatures in\nthe upper 90s to low 100s across most of the Great Basin. This\nwill not only lead to heat-related illness concerns for the\nelderly and those susceptible to the heat, but to anyone who\nspends time outdoors, especially in the sun. Consider postponing\noutdoor activities until the morning or late evening. Drink plenty\nof fluids, wear loose-fitting clothing, and take frequent breaks \nif you must be outdoors. Heat Advisories are likely to continue \nfor portions of the area into early next week, though a slight\nreprieve arrives on Sunday across northern Nevada as a weak \n\"cold\" front drops south out of Oregon and Idaho with the \naforementioned shortwave trough that moves across the Pacific \nNorthwest into the northern Rockies. Moisture will be limited with\nthis so no thunderstorm activity is expected.\n\nHere are the probabilities for highs to top the century mark on\nSaturday:\n\nBattle Mountain - 90%\nCarlin - 85%\nElko - 85%\nWinnemucca - 85%\nWest Wendover - 85%\nWells - 90%\nSpring Creek - 75%\nTonopah - 65%\nEureka - 70%\nEly - 35%\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in hot and dry weather continuing through the \nweekend and into the early part of next week. High forecast \nconfidence regarding a moderate risk of heat-related illnesses for\nheat-sensitive groups each afternoon through Sunday. High \nforecast confidence in above normal temperatures persisting into \nat least the middle of next week. Medium confidence in elevated to\nnear-critical fire weather conditions across northern Nevada \nduring the afternoon periods Saturday through Monday with timing \nof strongest wind gusts coinciding with minimum RH values \nremaining more uncertain.",
